expect Long thread starts here
# Look: oldest first at the top, no message twice across the pages' seams (#70/#71, #20/#21), no jump.
shot long-thread-top
swipe 0.5 0.85 0.5 0.3 300
wait 600
shot long-thread-seam
# The Mac stopped: the inbox says so and keeps what it has.
[phone] With the real service on the MacBook: link from the phone-link file (Taildropped), chats and names are Boss's own, one plain-text send to a chat he picks arrives on his other devices, a reply from him shows within seconds.
[phone] Mac locked: one plain text and one tapback (later slice) still go; note which don't.
[phone] Hold a message from someone: the six tapbacks show above Reply/Copy; tapping one puts it under the message here and on the Mac; tapping it again takes it off.
[phone] Open a long chat with a friend and scroll to the top: older messages keep coming past the first 50, in order, with nothing twice.
